# Docker build-context exclusions (Phase 5, PLAN.md §11 / §4).
# Keeps dependency trees, virtualenvs, VCS/tooling metadata, secrets, and
# runtime data out of the build context and every image layer (ASVS V14).
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.next
.git
.planning
.claude
frontend/out
db/*.db
db/*.db-journal
# Unlike .gitignore, Docker anchors a slash-free pattern to the context
# root only, so a bare `.env` line never covered `.env.<suffix>` variants
# or a bare dotenv file below the root (05-REVIEW.md CR-01). The `**/`
# prefix matches zero or more directories, covering every depth, and
# protects both whole-directory copies in the Dockerfile (`COPY frontend/
# ./` in frontend-build, `COPY backend/app ./app` in runtime). It also
# keeps `next build` inside the image hermetic: Next.js loads `.env.local`
# and `.env.production*` during a production build and inlines any
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* value into the shipped static bundle, so a contributor's
# local file could otherwise change what the image serves. Order matters:
# Docker applies .dockerignore rules last-match-wins, so the re-include
# must come after the variant exclusion or the committed templates would
# be dropped too.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.log
